e; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open this cycle after incumbent Dusty Johnson retired to run for governor. Republican Marty Jackley, the state attorney general, won his primary decisively and has raised about $1.4 million with over $1 million on hand. Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised roughly $260,000 and trails badly in resources.\n\nThe state's strong Republican lean and prediction markets pricing Democratic chances near 4 percent frame this as a Republican-favored race. A single Democratic-sponsored poll from late August showed a surprisingly close 4-point contest, but it stands alone against otherwise lopsided fundamentals. The seat remains likely to stay in Republican hands, with some residual uncertainty from the thin polling record.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0301, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0189, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0369, "margin": -14.0}]}